1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Wang Suzhi 王肅之 (fl. 353–384). Eastern Jin poet.
2 CONT
2 CONT Wang Suzhi's ancestral home was Linyi 臨沂 in Langye 琅邪 commandery (modern Linyi, Shandong). He was the fourth son of Wang Xizhi 王羲之 (303–361). Little is known of the events of his life. He served as director of the secretariat. He 
2 CONC also participated in the Lan ting gathering of 353 hosted by his father in Guiji. When ca. 384, Fu Lang 苻朗 (d. 389) of the Former Qin state visited Jiankang, he became annoyed with Wang Suzhi, who peppered him with questions about
2 CONC  various people of the Central Plain area. The monograph on bibliography lists Wang Suzhi's collected works in three ''juan''. This was lost in the Tang. Only two of his literary works survive, two pieces he composed for the Lan t
2 CONC ing gathering.
2 CONT
2 CONT DRK
