2 CONT * Lee, Lily Xiao Hong. “Xie Daoyun: The Style of a Woman Mingshi.” In Lily Xiao Hong Lee. Virtue of Yin: Studies on Chinese Women, 25–46. Sydney: Wild Peony, 1994. 
2 CONT * Li Jingqi 李景琦. “Yong xu cai gao linxia feng qing—Dong Jin cainü mingshi Xie Daoyun” 詠絮才高林下風清—東晉才女、名士謝道韞. Wenshi zhishi (1994: 4): 46–49. 
2 CONT * Chen Liao 陳遼. “Xie Daoyun shengzu nian kao” 謝道韞生卒年考. Wenjiao ziliao (1998: 6): 90–91. 
2 CONT * Ding Fulin 丁福林. Dong Jin Nanbeichao de Xieshi wenxue jituan 東晉南北朝的謝氏文學集團, 39–41. Harbin: Heilongjiang jiaoyu chubanshe, 1999. 
2 CONT * Xu Gongchi. Wei Jin wenxue shi, 537–38. 
2 CONT * Yang Hesong 楊賀松. “Celebrated Poetess Xie Daoyun.” Zhongguo funü (2001: 4): 19–20. 
2 CONT * Chen Xihong 陳希紅. “Xie Daoyun shengzu nian kao” 謝道韞生卒年考. Jiang Huai luntan (2003: 1): 127–29. 
2 CONT * Cao Daoheng and Shen Yucheng. Zhonggu wenxue shiliao congkao, 22–25. 
2 CONT * Idema, Wilt and Beata Grant. The Red Brush: Writing Women of Imperial China, 136–44. Cambridge: Harvard University Asia Center, 2004. 
2 CONT * Lee, Lily Xiao Hong. “Xie Daoyun.” In Biographical Dictionary of Chinese Women: Antiquity through Sui 1600 b.c.e.–618 c.e., ed. Lily Xiao Hong Lee and A.D. Stefanowska, 359–63. Armonk, N.Y.: M.E. Sharpe, 2007. 
2 CONT * Lu Xiaping 盧夏平. “Linxia zhi feng yong xu cai—ping Xie Daoyun de xuanxueguan ji qi shiwen chuangzuo” 林下之風詠絮才—評謝道韞的玄學觀及其詩文 創作. Zhangzhou shifan xueyuan xuebao (Zhexue shehui kexue ban) 67.1 (2008): 72–74. 
2 CONT * Zeng Caihua 曾彩華. “Xie Daoyun shengzu nian buzheng” 謝道韞生卒年補正. Liuzhou shizhuan xuebao 25.1 (2010): 43–49.
2 CONT
