1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://cbdb.fas.harvard.edu/cbdbapi/person.php?id=18763 '''Xue Chuguba''' 薛初古拔] [18763] XTS, 73B.25a-25b. His mingzi was Hong or Honglong, which is the one used in the XTS genealogy and Chuguba is treated as his 
2 CONC zi, but Chuguba was the Turkish mingzi granted by the Wei emperor, Taiwu di, who also made him Duke of Hedong (Hedong gong). Renming Da cidian, p. 1665. See also documentation for his ancestor, Guangde [18740]. — [https://www.geni
2 CONC .com/projects/CBDB-Hartwell-collection/46406 RMH]
