1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Xie Zhen 謝貞 (534–585), ''zi'' Yuanzheng 元正. Liang and Chen period literatus.
2 CONT
2 CONT Xie Zhen's ancestral home was Yangjia 陽夏 in Chen 陳 commandery (modern Taikang 太康, Henan). He was the ninth-generation descendant of Xie An 謝安 (320–385). His father Xie Lin 謝藺 (510–547) was a prominent figure during the late Liang 
2 CONC period. Like his father, Xie Zhen was also known for his filial piety. When Xie Lin died in 547, Xie Zhen, who was only fourteen years old, grieved excessively. When the Hou Jing insurrection broke out in 548, Xie Zhen's relatives
2 CONC  fled. In 554, Xie Zhen was in Jiangling when it was invaded by the forces of the Western Wei. Xie Zhen was captured and taken north to the Western Wei capital of Chang'an. During the Northern Zhou he served as reader-in-waiting f
2 CONC or the Prince of Zhao Yuwen Zhao 宇文招 (d. 580). In 572, Yuwen Zhao was assigned as governor of Yongzhou 雍州 (administrative seat, Xiangyang). Moved by Xie's longing to return home to care for his mother, he requested permission from
2 CONC  the Zhou court to allow Xie to travel south to Jiankang with the Zhou emisssary Du Gao 杜杲 (d. 582). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Upon his return to the Chen court, Xie Zhen was appointed administrator of the Section for Outer Troops in the establishment of the Wise and Martial General. He then was assigned as recorder on the staff of Chen Shuling 陳叔陵 (d. 58
2 CONC 2), Prince of Shixing. Seeing that Chen Shuling had designs on seizing the imperial throne, Xie Zhen and Ruan Zhuo 阮卓  (n.d.) distanced themselves from him. Chen Shuling tried to murder his brother Chen Shubao 陳叔寶 (553–564) on 18 
2 CONC February 582, but both Xie Zhen and Ruan Zhuo refused to participated in the plot. After Chen Shuling's murder attempt failed, and Chen Shubao ascended the imperial throne on 20 February, Xie Zhen was placed in charge of the admin
2 CONC istration of the palace of the empress. When Xie Zhen's mother passed away in 585, Xie soon died thereafter of excessive mourning.
2 CONT
2 CONT Already in his youth Xie Zhen displayed unusual intelligence and learning. His mother taught him the ''Lun yu'' and ''Xiao jing''. At the age of eight he composed a poem titled “Dwelling in Leisure on a Spring Day” that met with p
2 CONC raise from Wang Yun 王筠 (481–549). During the Chen period, Zhou Que 周確 was appointed to the position of minister in the section for justice of the Department of State Affairs. He asked Xie Zhen to compose the petition declining the
2 CONC  position. Xie's collected works were lost in the turmoil of the warfare at the end of the Liang.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bibliography
2 CONT
2 CONT Studies
2 CONT
2 CONT * Cao Daoheng and Shen Yucheng, Zhongguo wenxuejia dacidian, 445–46. 
2 CONT * Ding Fulin 丁福林. Dong Jin Nanchao Xieshi wenxue jituan 東晉南朝謝氏文學集團, 266–68. Harbin: Heilongjiang jiaoyu chubanshe, 1998.
2 CONT
